<title>ESTONIA: HOIUPANK SIGNS 400MLN EEK BOND ISSUE AGREEMENT.</title>
<headline>HOIUPANK SIGNS 400MLN EEK BOND ISSUE AGREEMENT.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hoiupank, Estonia's third largest bank, said on Thursday that it had signed an agreement for a 400 million kroon bond issue with Credit Suisse First Boston on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The interest on the three-year bonds will be the German mark Libor plus 0.75 percent, the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>As part of the agreement Hoiupank will also take a 160 million kroon subordinated loan for a term of seven years.</p>
<p>The bank earlier said that the bond issue would be used to assist its growth and to refinance some existing loans.</p>
<p>--David Mardiste, Tallinn newsroom +372 630 8400 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
